-- An `Alternative` keeps references to its guards' variables; keep them alive while it is used. It is
-  not copyable.
+- **A binding belongs to the `Alternative` that takes it.** The `Alternative` keeps the address of
+  each guard's variable: keep the variable alive while the `Alternative` is used (a loop-local variable
+  is fine for an `Alternative` built in the same loop iteration). Several `Alternative`s of a process
+  may bind the same channel end, with the same or with different variables; each reads into (writes
+  from) its own (3.2.0). Up to 3.1.0 the binding made last decided the variable for all of them, so
+  there bind an end to one variable only
+  ([known issues](https://github.com/OliverFaust/CSP4CMSIS/blob/main/docs/known-issues.md)). One
+  channel end bound twice in one `Alternative` is a fatal error (3.2.0). An `Alternative` is not
+  copyable.
 
